Near miss for begincase_requires_case: a :BEGINCASE with no :CASE that
never reaches :ENDCASE. The rule is emitted at close, so only
unclosed_block reports the opener; begincase_requires_case must NOT fire
(catalog "must NOT flag" second bullet). Because the block stays open,
the :RETURN after the :OTHERWISE branch's :EXITCASE is read as part of
that branch and exitcase_last_in_branch also fires on it: a consequence
of the same missing :ENDCASE.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE PickBin;
	:PARAMETERS nSize;
	:DECLARE sBin;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:OTHERWISE;
		sBin := "default";
		:EXITCASE;
	:RETURN sBin;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE PickBin;
	:PARAMETERS nSize;
	:DECLARE sBin;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:OTHERWISE;
		sBin := "default";
		:EXITCASE;
		:RETURN sBin;
	:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:12 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':BEGINCASE' - expected ':ENDCASE'
8:2-8:9 error exitcase_last_in_branch: Statement after ':EXITCASE' does not compile: ':EXITCASE' must be the last statement of its ':CASE' or ':OTHERWISE' branch
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:14-2:19 hint unused_variable: Variable 'nSize' is declared but never used
4:2-4:12 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':BEGINCASE' - expected ':ENDCASE'
8:2-8:9 error exitcase_last_in_branch: Statement after ':EXITCASE' does not compile: ':EXITCASE' must be the last statement of its ':CASE' or ':OTHERWISE' branch
